<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ban Mueang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Pho Khun Ban Mueang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ban Mueang was the second king of Sukhothai, the elder son of its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/si-inthrathit">Si Inthrathit</a>. According to the inscription attributed to his younger brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ram-khamhaeng">Ram Khamhaeng</a>, he succeeded his father and ruled while Ram Khamhaeng served as a commander. He was succeeded by Ram Khamhaeng, probably around 1279, and little else is known of his reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ban-mueang.jpg" alt="Ban Mueang" width="320" height="567" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ananda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phra_Ruang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
